Description: AI-native, Rust-based desktop shell for Ubuntu
 Umoja is a resilient, modern desktop environment built in Rust, powered by
 Mir and GTK4. It features seamless GNOME/Ubuntu settings fidelity,
 Myna voice dictation, and an embedded Lemonade AI search assistant.
 .
 The Lemonade server is bundled privately under /usr/lib/umoja/lemonade and
 runs per user on 127.0.0.1:13345, so it does not conflict with a system
 lemonade-server package on its default port 13305.
 .
 umoja-panel is the session's polkit authentication agent and notification
 server, which is what lets update-manager, update-notifier and
 nm-connection-editor install without GNOME Shell.
 .
 Without GNOME Shell, the Ubuntu Dock and Tiling Assistant settings that
 Umoja and Settings > Ubuntu Desktop use have no schemas, so umoja-desktop
 carries a copy in /usr/share/umoja/gsettings, used only when
 gnome-shell-ubuntu-extensions isn't installed.

Package: umoja-greeter
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         debconf,
         lightdm (>= 1.30),
         umoja-desktop (= ${binary:Version}),
         accountsservice,
         ubuntu-wallpapers
Recommends: xserver-xorg-core,
            xauth,
            libpam-fprintd
Provides: lightdm-greeter
Description: GTK4 LightDM greeter for Umoja
 A login screen for LightDM, written in Rust and GTK4, drawn over a
 softened copy of Ubuntu's default wallpaper. It lists users from
 AccountsService, supports session selection and user switching, and
 preselects the Umoja session.
 .
 On a fresh install this package makes LightDM the default display manager
 in place of GDM; the change takes effect at the next boot. Removing the
 package restores the previous display manager.

Package: ubuntu-umoja-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${umoja:Depends},
         umoja-desktop (>= ${source:Version}),
         umoja-greeter (>= ${source:Version}),
         umoja-archive-keyring
Recommends: ${umoja:Recommends}
Conflicts: budgie-desktop,
           gdm3,
           gnome-shell
Description: Ubuntu with the Umoja desktop (metapackage)
 Everything Ubuntu Desktop installs by default, with Umoja in place of
 GNOME Shell: the Umoja shell and greeter instead of gnome-shell, gdm3 and
 the Ubuntu GNOME session. GNOME apps, Settings, portals, Yaru and the
 Ubuntu defaults stay. Also adds Showtime and Snapshot.
 .
 The lists follow ubuntu-desktop-minimal; packaging/meta/update in the
 Umoja source refreshes them. It conflicts with gnome-shell, gdm3 and
 budgie-desktop because xdg-desktop-portal-gnome recommends
 "gnome-shell | budgie-desktop", which would otherwise bring back GNOME
 Shell, GDM and the Ubuntu GNOME session, or the Budgie desktop. To keep
 GNOME or Budgie next to Umoja, install umoja-desktop instead.

Package: umoja-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Package source and signing key for the Umoja PPA
 Adds ppa:ken-vandine/umoja as a package source, with its signing key, so
 Umoja and its patched Mir keep updating after install. Mir packages from
 the PPA are pinned above the Ubuntu archive's, since Umoja needs its
 patches. If the PPA is already configured (add-apt-repository), the
 existing source is left alone. The edge PPA is never enabled by this
 package.
